                <pb facs="0512" n="498" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg498"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. McCulloch, collector, to Mr. Lowry, surveyor.</hi>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Custom-House,
                            Baltimore</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Collector’s
                        Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1819-11-15"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">November</hi> 15, 1819</date>.</dateline>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Please to direct two officers of inspection
                    to examine, visit, and report to this office all and every privateer or ship of
                    war under foreign colors. Take an account of every particular of armament; the
                    number and description of crew—that is, what countrymen; under what commission
                    they sail, and whether their commission is lodged at the customhouse, and, if
                    not, demand it for depository here. From this last direction the brig
                    Independencia, Gunnalds, commander, is to be excepted, as I have lately had his
                    commission and know her to be a national vessel.</p>
                <p>The officers will please to report, with as much expedition as possible, adding
                    any remark of their own on the appearance or conduct of their crews or
                    commanders.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. H. McCULLOCH,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Collector.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wm. Lowry</hi>, Esq.,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Surveyor Port of Baltimore.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
